# Application Conventions

## UI / theme wiring

App shells that compose `@azes/ui-web` (theme, layout, nav, settings): follow
`.cursor/rules/uiDesignAgent.mdc` and update `docs/styles/CURRENT-STATE.md` when adoption or
chrome wiring changes. Product business logic stays in the app.

## API / Query wiring

App providers (`configureApi`, `QueryClient`, auth→API bridge) and feature hooks that call
`@azes/api` / `@azes/api/admin`: follow `.cursor/rules/apiMenecerAgent.mdc` and update
`docs/api/CURRENT-STATE.md` when runtime wiring or cache policy changes.

## Feature pages

Mandatory structure: `.cursor/rules/page-architecture.mdc` and
`docs/architecture/pages-and-features.md`. Thin `pages/<ad>/index.tsx` + fat
`features/<ad>/` (components, columns, hooks, service, models). API runtime protocol:
`.cursor/rules/apiMenecerAgent.mdc`. UI tokens/i18n: `.cursor/rules/ui-conventions.mdc`.
Canonical examples: `apps/admin` Users and Ads.

## Target apps

- Vite SPA: `account`, `admin`, `agent-platform`
- Next.js App Router: `realestate`, `agent-site` (dev :300), `real-estate-site` (dev :400)
- Expo (expo-router): `mobile-account`, `mobile-agent`, `mobile-realestate`

## Structure (create directories only when needed)

```text
apps/<app>/
├── src/ (or app/ for Next.js)
│   ├── components/
│   ├── features/      # only when a feature exists
│   ├── providers/
│   ├── lib/
│   └── config/
├── public/            # web only, when needed
└── package.json
```

Do not create empty placeholder directories.

## Rules

- Product-specific business logic stays in the app (`features/`). Do not move it to packages
  until multiple products genuinely need it.
- Apps may import `@azes/*` packages. Apps must NOT import other apps.
- Consume UI only via `@azes/ui-web` or `@azes/ui-native` — never third-party UI libraries.
- First-phase shells: Home page/screen only. No auth UI, dashboards, property/agent/admin
  features, real API workflows, or complex navigation unless the approved phase explicitly
  requires them.
- Next.js-specific infra stays in `apps/realestate` — do not push App Router concerns into
  generic packages.
- Mobile apps use Expo patterns; do not force web abstractions onto Native.

See `docs/architecture/application-architecture.md`.
